WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.672 --> 00:00:11.949
This is shelf, a small Python project.

2
00:00:11.949 --> 00:00:14.363
Start imece in its checkout.

3
00:00:15.873 --> 00:00:22.180
The first time, a welcome window says Claude Code is signed in, and lists the keys

4
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.257
to start with.

5
00:00:23.257 --> 00:00:24.564
Escape closes it.

6
00:00:34.174 --> 00:00:38.909
Press slash, and tell the leader what you want, in your own words.

7
00:00:38.909 --> 00:00:39.985
Enter sends it.

8
00:00:51.674 --> 00:00:56.045
The leader reads the code, and hires a worker for the task.

9
00:01:00.372 --> 00:01:04.542
When the worker is done, its change waits for you.

10
00:01:04.542 --> 00:01:11.463
The first line is the verdict: the tests ran on exactly this change, and every file

11
00:01:11.463 --> 00:01:13.047
is inside its card.

12
00:01:13.047 --> 00:01:14.799
Enter reads the diff.

13
00:01:14.799 --> 00:01:17.384
Tab shows its talk and its log.

14
00:01:25.473 --> 00:01:26.333
A approves.

15
00:01:26.333 --> 00:01:29.538
The change lands staged in your checkout.

16
00:01:29.538 --> 00:01:31.805
Nothing is committed for you.

17
00:01:37.275 --> 00:01:41.341
Colon commit asks a cheap model for a message.

18
00:01:41.341 --> 00:01:44.966
Enter runs git commit, in your own shell.

19
00:01:57.976 --> 00:01:58.631
Q quits.

20
00:01:58.631 --> 00:02:03.867
The agents sleep, and the next start goes on where you left off.

21
00:02:08.676 --> 00:02:14.127
Install imece with one line, and start it in any git checkout.

